From: Djair Guilherme <djair.jr@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] driver core: fw_devlink: no error for a refused sync-state-only link

device_link_add() refuses a SYNC_STATE_ONLY link when the consumer has
already probed, by design. fw_devlink reported that as
"Failed to create device link (0x180) with supplier ..." at dev_err, e.g.
for the reset GPIO of the SDIO card node under the reCamera SD host,
whose GPIO controller registers after the host probes. Log that case
at debug level; behaviour and return value are unchanged.

diff --color -ruN a/drivers/base/core.c b/drivers/base/core.c
--- a/drivers/base/core.c	2026-10-18 15:54:37.478549491 -0300
+++ b/drivers/base/core.c	2026-10-18 15:54:37.493206170 -0300
@@ -2237,8 +2237,23 @@
 		}
 
 		if (con != sup_dev && !device_link_add(con, sup_dev, flags)) {
-			dev_err(con, "Failed to create device link (0x%x) with supplier %s for %pfwf\n",
-				flags, dev_name(sup_dev), link->consumer);
+			/*
+			 * device_link_add() refuses a SYNC_STATE_ONLY link once
+			 * the consumer has probed, by design ("useless once a
+			 * consumer device has probed").  That is the normal
+			 * outcome when a child node of an already bound device
+			 * references a supplier that registers later (e.g. the
+			 * reset GPIO of an SDIO card node under an MMC host), so
+			 * it is not an error.  Same return value as before.
+			 */
+			if ((flags & DL_FLAG_SYNC_STATE_ONLY) &&
+			    con->links.status != DL_DEV_NO_DRIVER &&
+			    con->links.status != DL_DEV_PROBING)
+				dev_dbg(con, "Not creating sync-state-only link with %s for %pfwf: consumer already bound\n",
+					dev_name(sup_dev), link->consumer);
+			else
+				dev_err(con, "Failed to create device link (0x%x) with supplier %s for %pfwf\n",
+					flags, dev_name(sup_dev), link->consumer);
 			ret = -EINVAL;
 		}
 
